concept :the_paired_month do
  name "The Paired Month"
  tags :prediction, :legibility, :surveillance, :governance

  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    One calendar month in each register year during which the roll at #{ref :tangwang_post, "Tangwang Post"} is measured twice in units that do not convert into each other, so that the rest of the year can be reported in one of them. The post's clinic files its ordinary roster figure — the aggregate the mesh takes off everybody inside it, and the same quantity #{ref :emotional_consensus, "a district's policy"} is read from. Alongside it, for that month only, the roll keeper writes a named sheet by hand: attendance, hours, refusals, days lost, and the compartments each crew closed.

    #{ref :continuity, "Continuity"}'s cabinet works the way #{ref :predictive_governance, "its models work everywhere"} — one person at a time — has no reading of its own on the Root's side of the world, and will not take a figure it cannot attribute. The named sheet gives it a month of attributable behaviour. Set against the clinic's series for the same thirty days, it yields a conversion the cabinet then applies to eleven months of aggregate.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :mechanics, heading: "Thirty-One Of Forty-Four"
    The conversion states the fraction it was built on, because the clinic's figure does not cover the roll. Forty-four names stood on the roll in the last register year and the roster aggregate covered thirty-one. Three contract scouts carry nothing that reports and stand down outside the post's #{ref :mycelial_neural_mesh, "mesh"} after a walk. Ten grid-hands from #{ref :sanchakou, "Sanchakou"} are paid by the day out of the settlement's account and belong to the settlement's mesh, not the post's.

    Two corrections are filed for the thirteen the clinic does not read, and they are not the same correction. The roll keeper scales the aggregate by the read fraction and enters the unread names at nothing. The cabinet weights them at the roll's mean, on the reasoning printed with the sheet: a name absent from a reading is not a name reading zero. The two figures run about a seventh apart, the wider gap belonging to the cabinet, and both go into the file with the month.

    A conversion is good for the roster it was built on. A crew rotated off an inland posting, a scout added to the roll, or a settlement's account taking over a grid line ends it, and the post carries the aggregate uncorrected until the next paired month comes round.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "What A Converted Figure Says About One Person"
    The conversion turns a figure describing a roll into a figure the cabinet reads as describing a name, and there is nothing in the arithmetic that makes the second true of anybody. Every entrant on the quarterly round into the band #{ref :the_ring_order, "a ring order"} reserves is scored before the round goes out, and for the thirteen the clinic does not read the score is the roll's mean with their own condition that week nowhere in it. #{ref :the_ninth_grid_hand, "The ninth grid-hand"} is the case the post argues from.

    Continuity's position, filed with the model and unchanged since 2088, is that a threshold applied to a converted figure is the honest use of a converted figure and the alternative is clearing entrants against no reading at all. #{ref :the_great_root, "The Great Root"}'s line service does not dispute the conversion and does not sign it. Its clinic states a figure to the person it was taken from and to no file, so a reading that would contradict a converted score cannot be put on the sheet that carries the score.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The whole procedure is built on the ecological fallacy and the correction literature around it: an inference from an aggregate to an individual, whose bias runs with the fraction of the population the aggregate actually sampled, and for which competing adjustment methods disagree by an amount that has to be reported alongside the estimate. That decided the shape — a stated read fraction, two corrections filed side by side, and a conversion invalidated by a change in the roster it was calibrated on."
end
